  "body": "Historical DAG downgrade tests could leave the database at an intermediate revision after the expected history guard refused the older downgrade. Subsequent setup then failed because the current cleanup expected routed-record columns.\n\nRestore the latest schema in `finally` and always dispose the engine in that one test. All original assertions, strict cleanup, production ORM and DDL remain unchanged.\n\nValidation: the architect independently ran all four historical migration modules on PostgreSQL 17 and SQLite: 90 passed on each backend, zero skips. The focused DAG module also passed 7/7 on both. The full hosted matrix, including PostgreSQL 14, must run again.\n\n[Evidence and original CI failure](https://github.com/Anacreonsystems/ariadne/blob/native-stream-storage/architecture/streaming-etl/evidence/native-epoch2-full-ci-schema-context-2026-11-05/index.json).\n",
  "changed_files": 95,
  "closed_at": "2026-11-05T09:14:32Z",
